('advanced-native-2064', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-2064-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["Staff describe continued curiosity as one reason to remain, while pay and conditions still matter."],"options":["The interviews say their interest has replaced the need to consider working conditions.","Staff describe continued curiosity as one reason to remain, while pay and conditions still matter.","The staff say they remain only because their pay is high and no longer find the work interesting.","The staff describe an initial attraction to the role, but give no reason for continuing to engage with it."]},"advanced-native-2064-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["Interest is often what keeps them in the room: they still want to explore new reading questions.","They find the questions worth pursuing, while still caring about pay and working conditions.","Their curiosity gives a reason to continue that is not just about the pay.","They describe wanting to learn more from the work, without saying the practical conditions no longer matter."],"options":["Interest is often what keeps them in the room: they still want to explore new reading questions.","They find the questions worth pursuing, while still caring about pay and working conditions.","Their curiosity gives a reason to continue that is not just about the pay.","They describe wanting to learn more from the work, without saying the practical conditions no longer matter."]},"advanced-native-2064-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["The phrase “interest is often what keeps them in the room” should not replace her stated reason for staying through the handover."],"options":["Remaining in the post is enough to show that she still finds the tasks interesting.","Her account identifies the prospect of new reading questions as the reason for continuing in the post.","The phrase “interest is often what keeps them in the room” should not replace her stated reason for staying through the handover."]},"advanced-native-2064-