('advanced-native-2065', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-2065-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["Pay may attract an initial application, while understanding the duties and selection still lie ahead."],"options":["The account says candidates choose only after completing a long period in the role.","The manager has said that duties do not need to be discussed once salary has attracted interest.","Pay may attract an initial application, while understanding the duties and selection still lie ahead.","Submitting an application already confirms that the candidate has accepted an offer."]},"advanced-native-2065-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["It may draw a candidate’s attention before they learn more about the duties.","The pay can encourage a first application without settling the selection result.","It can be an attraction at the start, rather than proof of a completed appointment.","Salary may get someone through the door by making an application worth considering."],"options":["It may draw a candidate’s attention before they learn more about the duties.","The pay can encourage a first application without settling the selection result.","It can be an attraction at the start, rather than proof of a completed appointment.","Salary may get someone through the door by making an application worth considering."]},"advanced-native-2065-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["Saying salary may get someone through the door does not establish that pay prompted this application; the stated sequence gives another initial reason."],"options":["Saying salary may get someone through the door does not establish that pay prompted this application; the stated sequence gives another initial reason.","The account says the applicant compared the salary before deciding to submit.","The applicant identifies pay as the reason for the first application and the work as a later discovery."]},"advanced-native-2065-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["The person has already passed selection and will certainly remain in the job."],"options":["Pay can be an initial attraction to a job opportunity.","The person has already passed selection and will certainly remain in the job.","Further context can identify what the initial entry actually involves."]},"advanced-native-2065-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["Salary may get someone through the door, but we still need to explain the duties and let candidates ask whether the role fits before they decide."],"options":["Salary may get someone through the door, but we still need to explain the duties and let candidates ask whether the role fits before they decide.","I would leave the rota discussion until after acceptance, since the salary has already attracted attention.","I would treat the number of applications as confirmation that the candidates understand the work."]},"advanced-native-2065-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["Salary may get someone through the door, but the withdrawals do not tell us why these candidates left. Could we offer an optional follow-up asking what shaped their decision, without requiring a reply or labelling them all as dissatisfied with pay?","The salary may get someone through the door without explaining a later withdrawal. I suggest inviting those candidates to share their reasons voluntarily and recording each response as their own experience, rather than assuming one cause for the group."],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
('advanced-native-2066', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-2066-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["The attraction of the promised payment made leaving harder, because receiving it depended on staying until the season ended."],"options":["Maya would receive the same promised payment on the same terms even if she left immediately.","The payment was described as reimbursement for a completed expense, unrelated to how long she stayed.","Maya had stopped considering another role and said that the work itself was now her main reason to remain.","The attraction of the promised payment made leaving harder, because receiving it depended on staying until the season ended."]},"advanced-native-2066-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["She had to consider the attractive payment alongside her wish to move on.","The incentive gave her a reason to delay leaving that was separate from liking the work.","It felt like golden handcuffs because leaving before the season ended meant missing the payment she was considering.","The benefit was tied to remaining until the end, even though she wanted a different role."],"options":["She had to consider the attractive payment alongside her wish to move on.","The incentive gave her a reason to delay leaving that was separate from liking the work.","It felt like golden handcuffs because leaving before the season ended meant missing the payment she was considering.","The benefit was tied to remaining until the end, even though she wanted a different role."]},"advanced-native-2066-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["A large reimbursement alone does not establish golden handcuffs when this account does not tie it to remaining in the job."],"options":["The account describes a bonus available only to staff who remain until the next season.","The reimbursement is presented as payment for accepting future duties, rather than expenses already incurred.","A large reimbursement alone does not establish golden handcuffs when this account does not tie it to remaining in the job."]},"advanced-native-2066-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["A legal rule physically or absolutely prevented the person from leaving."],"options":["More context is needed to know the actual terms and choices.","The attractive benefits made leaving feel difficult.","A legal rule physically or absolutely prevented the person from leaving."]},"advanced-native-2066-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["Golden handcuffs describes the incentive here, not a rule forbidding departure; we should state the season-end condition without inventing further restrictions."],"options":["I would describe the promised bonus as a legal ban on leaving, without checking whether the story says that.","I would treat a wish to leave as proof that the promised payment has no influence on the decision.","Golden handcuffs describes the incentive here, not a rule forbidding departure; we should state the season-end condition without inventing further restrictions."]},"advanced-native-2066-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["The bonus has felt like golden handcuffs, but I have decided to leave before the season ends because the new hours fit our family needs better. I know that means giving up this reward, and I have included that loss in my decision.","I am choosing to leave the golden handcuffs behind, knowing that an early departure means I will not receive the season-end payment. The reward matters, but after comparing the hours with our family needs I prefer the new role."],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
('advanced-native-2067', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-2067-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["The work could be tiring while she still found enjoyment and energy for her own drawing."],"options":["The work could be tiring while she still found enjoyment and energy for her own drawing.","She described a job with no tiring days and no difficult tasks.","She said the salary was the only valued part and that she had stopped wanting to draw.","The account gives only the studio’s pay figure, without describing how she experienced the work."]},"advanced-native-2067-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["The account links work with enjoyment and a continuing personal practice, not pay alone.","It paid the rent without draining the soul, since she still enjoyed the collaboration and her own drawing.","The income came alongside useful collaboration and energy for something she valued outside the job.","She did not have to describe every day as easy to find the work rewarding."],"options":["The account links work with enjoyment and a continuing personal practice, not pay alone.","It paid the rent without draining the soul, since she still enjoyed the collaboration and her own drawing.","The income came alongside useful collaboration and energy for something she valued outside the job.","She did not have to describe every day as easy to find the work rewarding."]},"advanced-native-2067-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["High pay alone does not show work continuing without draining the soul when the person describes a loss of meaning and interest."],"options":["High pay alone does not show work continuing without draining the soul when the person describes a loss of meaning and interest.","The account describes her enjoying the work and returning eagerly to her personal writing.","The person’s own experience is not relevant once the salary has been described as high."]},"advanced-native-2067-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["The person never feels tired or faces a demanding day."],"options":["The person never feels tired or faces a demanding day.","The surrounding account can explain what remains meaningful to the person.","The description avoids a figurative loss of meaning or vitality."]},"advanced-native-2067-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["Continuing without draining the soul depends on what she can actually sustain; enjoying the work is not agreement to extra evenings, so we should ask."],"options":["I would use her enjoyment as agreement to the extra rota before discussing her availability.","I would judge whether the extra work suits her only by the pay, rather than ask about its effect on her own time.","Continuing without draining the soul depends on what she can actually sustain; enjoying the work is not agreement to extra evenings, so we should ask."]},"advanced-native-2067-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["I want to keep doing this paid work without draining the soul, so could we discuss rotating reception duties and restoring an agreed drawing session? I value the workshop, but the current rota has left no time for the creative part I joined to do.","The work matters to me, but I need a way to continue without draining the soul. Could we look together at reception cover and the drawing time we agreed, before assuming the present allocation can continue unchanged?"],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
('advanced-native-2068', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-2068-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["The concern was power being displayed as its own purpose, while coordination could still be necessary."],"options":["The account describes removing an unnecessary approval step rather than adding one.","The concern was power being displayed as its own purpose, while coordination could still be necessary.","The narrator said shared equipment should have no coordinating arrangements at all.","The chair explained a specific equipment conflict that the extra approval would resolve."]},"advanced-native-2068-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["It appeared to be authority for its own sake, justified only by displaying who was in charge.","The stated reason did not identify a shared practical need for another step.","The concern was the purpose of the control, not the existence of every coordinating rule.","The narrator wanted a reason beyond showing the chair’s position."],"options":["It appeared to be authority for its own sake, justified only by displaying who was in charge.","The stated reason did not identify a shared practical need for another step.","The concern was the purpose of the control, not the existence of every coordinating rule.","The narrator wanted a reason beyond showing the chair’s position."]},"advanced-native-2068-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["A bounded return record with a stated shared purpose is not by itself authority for its own sake."],"options":["The account gives no reason for the signature beyond showing the manager’s rank.","The rule is described as requiring approval for choices unrelated to borrowed equipment.","A bounded return record with a stated shared purpose is not by itself authority for its own sake."]},"advanced-native-2068-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["The speaker must reject any leadership, coordination or useful rule."],"options":["The speaker objects to power being treated as its own purpose.","The speaker must reject any leadership, coordination or useful rule.","A concrete context can distinguish justified oversight from control without a relevant purpose."]},"advanced-native-2068-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["We should ask what the extra step achieves; questioning authority for its own sake does not stop us keeping a rule that serves a clear shared need."],"options":["I would remove the existing return record as well, without considering the equipment-sharing reason already given.","We should ask what the extra step achieves; questioning authority for its own sake does not stop us keeping a rule that serves a clear shared need.","I would keep the extra step on the strength of the title, without asking what problem it addresses."]},"advanced-native-2068-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["He crossed out the colour-approval line, recognising that he had been seeking authority for its own sake rather than helping the posters get made. The designers could choose their colours, while the agreed check of dates and venue details remained.","His fear of looking unnecessary had turned the colour choice into authority for its own sake, so he handed that decision back to the designers. He kept the shared facts check, this time able to explain what it was for."],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
('advanced-native-2069', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-2069-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["The team should examine doubtful captions and give reasons, while keeping an agreed deadline."],"options":["The editor withdrew the deadline so that the team would never need to coordinate the issue.","The editor asked for agreement without allowing the team to explain why a caption seemed doubtful.","The team should examine doubtful captions and give reasons, while keeping an agreed deadline.","The team should accept every caption because the editor’s title makes checking unnecessary."]},"advanced-native-2069-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["The team could question the wording and explain what evidence supported a change.","She kept a shared deadline while asking people to think about what they published.","Working together meant giving reasons, not accepting a caption merely because someone senior supplied it.","She wanted reasoned participation, not blind obedience to doubtful captions."],"options":["The team could question the wording and explain what evidence supported a change.","She kept a shared deadline while asking people to think about what they published.","Working together meant giving reasons, not accepting a caption merely because someone senior supplied it.","She wanted reasoned participation, not blind obedience to doubtful captions."]},"advanced-native-2069-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["Following a rule after asking about and understanding its purpose is not by itself blind obedience."],"options":["Following a rule after asking about and understanding its purpose is not by itself blind obedience.","The account says he filled the form without considering why it was needed.","The volunteer rejected the return record and refused any shared procedure."]},"advanced-native-2069-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["The person must reject every instruction even after understanding a useful reason for it."],"options":["The context can show how questions and cooperation coexist.","The person wants room to examine reasons and consequences.","The person must reject every instruction even after understanding a useful reason for it."]},"advanced-native-2069-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["Respect does not require blind obedience; we can explain a doubt about the evidence and still work towards the shared deadline."],"options":["I would avoid raising a doubtful date because agreeing with the editor matters more than checking this caption.","I would refuse the agreed deadline before discussing whether the caption itself can be checked.","Respect does not require blind obedience; we can explain a doubt about the evidence and still work towards the shared deadline."]},"advanced-native-2069-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["Blind obedience to the old form has turned missing values into zeros, so the report no longer shows which figures are unknown. I suggest marking those entries as unknown for now and asking the process owner to confirm how missing data should be handled.","We should replace blind obedience to the numeric-only instruction with a documented way to record missing data. Could we flag the affected entries as unknown and ask for an approved procedure, while keeping the checks on the figures we actually have?"],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
('advanced-native-2070', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-2070-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["She helps the group compare possible routes against a shared purpose without making every step herself."],"options":["The image is used only to describe the physical object in a shop display, with no leadership meaning.","The group has already completed the project, and the leader is only checking which route was fastest.","She helps the group compare possible routes against a shared purpose without making every step herself.","The essay describes her requiring the group to follow each of her choices without comparison."]},"advanced-native-2070-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["She gives orientation while leaving routes to be compared together.","The group has guidance without having every practical choice made for it.","Her questions connect possible actions with what the group is trying to achieve.","It pictures her as someone holding a compass, helping the group keep its purpose in view."],"options":["She gives orientation while leaving routes to be compared together.","The group has guidance without having every practical choice made for it.","Her questions connect possible actions with what the group is trying to achieve.","It pictures her as someone holding a compass, helping the group keep its purpose in view."]},"advanced-native-2070-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["A photograph of someone holding a compass can be literal; it does not by itself establish the guiding role imagined in the leadership comparison."],"options":["Possession of the object is enough to establish how he listens to the people he leads.","A photograph of someone holding a compass can be literal; it does not by itself establish the guiding role imagined in the leadership comparison.","The label already describes him helping a team compare actions against a shared aim."]},"advanced-native-2070-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["The leader has already guaranteed the result and made every later choice unnecessary."],"options":["The leader has already guaranteed the result and made every later choice unnecessary.","The context should explain what purpose or questions provide direction.","The image can suggest orientation towards a shared purpose."]},"advanced-native-2070-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["The image of someone holding a compass is about orientation; we still need to compare what each option does for our shared aim."],"options":["The image of someone holding a compass is about orientation; we still need to compare what each option does for our shared aim.","I would use her preferred answer as the whole explanation, without discussing how it fits the aim.","I would ignore her questions because making our own choice means accepting no guidance."]},"advanced-native-2070-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["Could we picture the coordinator as someone holding a compass, with members comparing their own route sketches beside her? The caption could name the shared purpose without suggesting she has already chosen every step for them.","I suggest a figure holding a compass to represent orientation, alongside several members discussing possible routes. Let the caption connect their choices with the shared aim, rather than promise a single route that cannot fail."],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
('advanced-native-2071', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-2071-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["The supervisor used a sharp manner and shut down questions while the updated information was still missing."],"options":["The account concerns only the list’s contents, with no description of the supervisor’s tone.","The supervisor used a sharp manner and shut down questions while the updated information was still missing.","The supervisor calmly supplied the revised list and invited the crew to check it.","The crew had the revised list and were discussing it without interruption."]},"advanced-native-2071-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["The supervisor began to bark orders and cut off the crew’s questions.","The response was sharp and left little space to clarify the missing list.","The supervisor snapped at people rather than first supplying the updated information.","The account describes a harsh delivery, not just a clear instruction."],"options":["The supervisor began to bark orders and cut off the crew’s questions.","The response was sharp and left little space to clarify the missing list.","The supervisor snapped at people rather than first supplying the updated information.","The account describes a harsh delivery, not just a clear instruction."]},"advanced-native-2071-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["Raising her voice to be heard does not by itself show that she barked orders; the account also describes respectful explanation and questions."],"options":["The instruction is described as inaudible to distant participants rather than deliberately made clearer.","Raising her voice to be heard does not by itself show that she barked orders; the account also describes respectful explanation and questions.","The account says she snapped at people and refused to hear any question."]},"advanced-native-2071-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["Every factual detail in the commands was therefore false."],"options":["More context can explain what he said and how 